Chapter: GpuDepthTree
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites UI chapter Theme
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites UI chapter Layout
  cites UI chapter BoxModel
  cites UI chapter GpuRender

 A child widget must render IN FRONT of its parent, and a gauge's fill in
 front of its own track.

 The rasterizer keeps a pixel only if its depth is strictly less than the
 one already stored, so geometry drawn at the depth of a fill that already
 covers it is discarded. Draw a whole widget tree at one depth and only the
 root survives. Nothing in the triangle count can see this: the losing
 rects are submitted and counted exactly as the winning ones are, which is
 why the GuiOS desktop reported twenty-two triangles a frame while painting
 nothing but its own background. The instrument has to read pixels.

 So this renders a panel containing a separator and a gauge, then counts
 framebuffer pixels of each child's colour. The panel paints pal-bg, the
 separator pal-border, the gauge fill pal-primary -- three distinct values
 in theme-terminal, which is what makes the children legible against their
 parent. Both counts are ZERO when the depth rule is broken, and the test
 was run against a compiler without the fix to confirm exactly that.

 The scan strides eight columns and every row: a separator is one pixel
 tall and spans nearly the full width, so a column stride finds it and a
 row stride could miss it. Counting is deliberate rather than sampling one
 computed coordinate -- it does not have to know where layout put anything,
 so it stays honest when the layout changes.

Section: Body

  fb-base : Integer = #BF000000
  fb-w : Integer = 640
  fb-h : Integer = 480

  scan-row : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  scan-row (y) (x) (target) (acc) =
    if x >= fb-w then acc
    else scan-row y (x + 8) target (acc + (if peek-32 fb-base ((y * fb-w + x) * 4) == target then 1 else 0))

  scan-fb : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  scan-fb (y) (target) (acc) =
    if y >= fb-h then acc
    else scan-fb (y + 1) target (acc + scan-row y 0 target 0)

  probe-tree : WidgetNode
  probe-tree =
    widget-panel "root" DirColumn 4 [
      widget-separator "sep",
      widget-set-min (widget-gauge "bar" 1 4) 0 40
    ]

  opening : [Gpu, Console] Nothing =
    act
      let th = theme-terminal
      in let pal = th.th-palette
      in let laid = widget-layout probe-tree th (layout-rect 0 0 fb-w fb-h)
      in act
        c1 <- gr-clear (pal.pal-bg)
        c2 <- gr-clear-depth
        n <- gr-flush ((gr-render-tree (gf-new 4096) laid th gr-depth-scene).gf-idx)
        print-line-uni ("separator: " & show (if scan-fb 0 (pal.pal-border) 0 > 0 then 1 else 0))
        print-line-uni ("gauge-fill: " & show (if scan-fb 0 (pal.pal-primary) 0 > 0 then 1 else 0))
      end
    end

